-- title:
--   Drinfeld's formal moduli of special formal mathcal O_D-modules
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $O^{nr}$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain which is a $\mathbb Z_q$-algebra, complete for the adic topology of the ideal generated by the image of $q$, that ideal being maximal, and with algebraically closed residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}(O^{nr})$. Let $\iota\colon W(\mathbb F_{q^2})\to O^{nr}$ be a ring homomorphism (here $W(\mathbb F_{q^2})$ is `Zp2 q`, the Witt vectors of the quadratic field with $q$ elements) and let $X_0$ be a `SpecialFormalODModule` over $k$ for the reduction of $\iota$: a two-dimensional commutative formal group law with a $W(\mathbb F_{q^2})$-action by endomorphisms and an endomorphism $\varpi$ satisfying $\varpi\circ\varpi=[q]$ and $\varpi\circ[a]=[\mathrm{Frob}(a)]\circ\varpi$, whose Lie algebra splits as a direct sum of the two invertible eigensummands `lieZero`, `lieOne`, and for which $[q]$ has kernel of degree $q^4$. Let $R$ be a Noetherian local $O^{nr}$-algebra, complete for its maximal-ideal adic topology, equipped with a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{res}_R\colon R\to k$ with $\mathrm{res}_R\circ(\text{structure map})$ the residue map of $O^{nr}$, let $X^u$ be a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $R$ (no specialness or height being assumed of it) and let $w^u$ be an isomorphism from $X^u$ base changed along $\mathrm{res}_R$ to $X_0$. Assume $(R,X^u,w^u)$ pro-represents the deformation problem: for every Artinian local $O^{nr}$-algebra $A$ with surjective $\mathrm{res}_A\colon A\to k$ compatible with the residue map of $O^{nr}$, every formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X$ over $A$ special for $\iota$ composed with the structure map and of height $4$, and every isomorphism $w$ from the reduction $X\otimes_A k$ to $X_0$, there is a unique $O^{nr}$-algebra homomorphism $\chi\colon R\to A$ such that $\mathrm{res}_A\circ\chi=\mathrm{res}_R$ and such that some isomorphism $v$ from $X^u$ base changed along $\chi$ to $X$ satisfies that the reduction of $v$ followed by $w$ has the same underlying series as $w^u$. Then $R$ is a regular local ring, the image of $q$ in $R$ is nonzero, and $R$ is isomorphic as an $O^{nr}$-algebra either to the one-variable power series ring $O^{nr}[[t]]$ or to [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel`](def/ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel.html#L15) of $O^{nr}$ at the image of $q$, the quotient of the two-variable power series ring over $O^{nr}$ by the ideal `uvCrossingIdeal`.
--
--   This is Drinfeld's determination of the formal moduli of a special formal $\mathcal O_D$-module of height $4$ over an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$: the deformation ring is the complete local ring of the formal model of the $q$-adic upper half plane at a smooth point or at an ordinary double point of its special fibre. Stated for an arbitrary pro-representing ring, it is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormalODModule.exists_isProrepresentedBy_deformations_powerSeries_or_uvCrossingModel`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormalODModule.exists_isProrepresentedBy_deformations_powerSeries_or_uvCrossingModel), and thence in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation input to the argument.
